The types of a beam-mode configuration (GENERATED by tools/bees_pack_gen.py; Silica has no type alias, so an
application spells them).

cfg (the value of (:ok, cfg)):
{ auth: { auth: string, cookie: string, redial: { initial_ms: int64, max_ms: int64, on: boolean }, transport: string }, links: List[{ address: string, host: string, how: { by_epmd: boolean, dials: boolean, port: int64, resolve: boolean }, name: string }, mem(normal)], net: { epmd: { mode: string, port: int64 }, listen_address: string, listen_port: int64, listener: string }, node: { creation: int64, name: string }, time: { frame_max: int64, io_ms: int64, open_ms: int64, tick_ms: int64 } }

reason (the value of (:error, reason)):
{ record: int64, schema: int64, text: string }

the reader actor's message to the application:
(:ok, { auth: { auth: string, cookie: string, redial: { initial_ms: int64, max_ms: int64, on: boolean }, transport: string }, links: List[{ address: string, host: string, how: { by_epmd: boolean, dials: boolean, port: int64, resolve: boolean }, name: string }, mem(normal)], net: { epmd: { mode: string, port: int64 }, listen_address: string, listen_port: int64, listener: string }, node: { creation: int64, name: string }, time: { frame_max: int64, io_ms: int64, open_ms: int64, tick_ms: int64 } }) | (:error, { record: int64, schema: int64, text: string })

groups:
index (schema 1, once): { frames: int64, kind: string, mode: string, version: int64 }
node (schema 2, once): { creation: int64, name: string }
net (schema 10, once): { epmd: { mode: string, port: int64 }, listen_address: string, listen_port: int64, listener: string }
time (schema 11, once): { frame_max: int64, io_ms: int64, open_ms: int64, tick_ms: int64 }
auth (schema 12, once): { auth: string, cookie: string, redial: { initial_ms: int64, max_ms: int64, on: boolean }, transport: string }
link (schema 13, many): { address: string, host: string, how: { by_epmd: boolean, dials: boolean, port: int64, resolve: boolean }, name: string }
